 ### Choosing a backend
 
+Durable writable activation also requires `storage-domain` and a ready native admission owner. SessionPersistence opens the canonical `session_lifecycle` domain and supplies the SessionStore admission gate used by ordinary, headless, and SDK compositions. A deleted or closing session cannot be recreated through another entry point. Free sessions require a matching directory ownership proof before writable activation; read-only inspection remains available. Backend reload or unavailable durable admission refuses activation until readiness returns. A composition without a persistence backend retains its stateless behavior.
+
 The seam ships the [JSONL](../session-persistence-jsonl/README.md) backend: one append-only `.jsonl.zstd` log per session. A third-party backend may implement the service directly; the [backend contract](#understand-the-implementation) below is what it must honor.
 
 ### What the service provides
