@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+---
+description: "Identity migration from Session V4 to V5 and native admission of classification, active-branch decisions, and host tool effects."
+kind: "package-library"
+---
+
+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-session-format-v4-to-v5
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Restore a released V4 Session as V5 without rewriting its events. The migration copies every event and marks the header `ordinary`. Native V5 admission accepts that header plus free-session ownership, active-branch decisions, and host tool-effect records. Persistence publishes the successor file; this library owns conversion and the V5 rules. A V4 reader still rejects a V5 file.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Use this package](#use-this-package)
+- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)
+- [Further Exploration](#further-exploration)
+- [Model Experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+-----
+
+<a id="use-this-package"></a>
+## Use this package
+
+### When to use it
+
+Use this package when a stored V4 log must be read by a V5 writer, or when a current writer must admit a V5 header and the two new event types. Do not copy the V4 codec. This package reuses `releasedV4SessionFormatCodec`.
+
+### Entry point
+
+| Export | Contract |
+|---|---|
+| `sessionFormatV4ToV5` | Adjacent identity migration. Events keep their sequence and payload. The target header is version 5 and `classification: "ordinary"`. |
+| `releasedV5SessionFormatCodec` | Current physical codec. Header version is 5. Rows are encoded with the V4 codec after V5 admission. |
+| `assertReleasedV5Header` | Requires `classification`. `free` requires absolute `ownedDirectory` equal to `cwd`. `ordinary` rejects `ownedDirectory`. |
+| `restoreReleasedV5Artifact` | Checks the V5 header, restores the V4 view, then checks active-branch and tool-effect payloads. |
+| `assertV5RowAdmission` | Runs V4 row admission, then checks `session/active-branch` and `host/tool-effect` when present. |
+
+<a id="understand-the-implementation"></a>
+## Understand the implementation
+
+`migrateHeader` calls `assertReleasedV4Header` and adds `classification: "ordinary"`. The stage copies events and runs. The inherited cut stays on the same `session/end-seed` marker. `releasedV5SessionFormatCodec` strips `classification` and `ownedDirectory`, delegates to the V4 codec, then stamps those fields back. V4 relationship checks see the stripped header, so a V5-only field cannot change V4 ownership rules.
+
+<a id="further-exploration"></a>
+## Further Exploration
+
+- [Session format status](../../../docs/session-format-status.md) — which writer version is current.
+- [V4 historical inventory](../../../docs/persistence-changes/historical-formats/v4.md) — the source this edge reads.
+- [V3 to V4](../session-format-v3-to-v4/README.md) — the codec this edge reuses.
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+### Historical restoration
+
+A restored V4 conversation is an ordinary session. Its prompts, tool results, and model-visible surface stay the same. Free classification and active-branch decisions exist only on logs written as V5. The model does not see the format version.
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+This edge does not allocate a free-session directory and does not delete sessions. Those actions belong to the session controller. It does not rewrite V4 bytes in place. A deployment that still writes V4 cannot read a V5 successor.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
